# Semgrep ignore list (gitignore syntax). Every entry needs a reason (.claude/rules/ground-rules.md).
#
# A custom .semgrepignore REPLACES Semgrep's built-in defaults. Verified 2026-10-04 with
# Semgrep 1.179.0: with only the codefixes/ line, 149 files under app/test/ and both *.min.js
# files were scanned. So the defaults that matter here are restated below.

# Coding-challenge answer options: read as text by routes/vulnCodeFixes.ts and
# routes/vulnCodeSnippet.ts and shown in the UI; never imported or executed. Findings there
# can't be exploited, and many files are fragments that don't parse (30 of 39 parse failures).
app/data/static/codefixes/

# Tests (app/test/ restates a default; *.spec.ts adds the frontend's unit tests). Gating rule 4
# excludes tests, and their fake tokens are already covered (and allowlisted) by Gitleaks.
app/test/
*.spec.ts

# Third-party code shipped as files, not first-party (*.min.js restates a default).
# three.js is a bundled copy of the three.js library: it fails to parse and caused all 3
# timeouts in the first scan.
*.min.js
app/frontend/src/assets/private/three.js

# Dependencies and build output (restated defaults). Not tracked in git, but listed in case a
# local scan runs after npm install or a frontend build.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
